summary:
  A relay writer that dies at birth sends only an audibly playing room back
  to the live stream, so a player still opening the tap is left on it.

history:
  Measured on the bench on 2026-11-11 with an MP3 stream the directory
  called FLAC: the tap answered 0.26 s after the start, ffmpeg refused the
  Ogg shell 0.09 s later, and the player, already sent to the tap and still
  opening it, did not count as playing. An audition stayed silent for the
  whole 25 s that were measured, and a saved station came back only with
  the heal road's knock, 15 s after the press.

target:
  package/contents/ui/TimeshiftEngine.qml

find:
                      if (backTo !== "" && !wasShifted && !app._tsPaused && (app.isPlaying() || onTap) && !app._orderLapsed())

replace:
                      if (backTo !== "" && !wasShifted && !app._tsPaused && app.isPlaying() && !app._orderLapsed())

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_timeshiftengine.qml::test_a_player_still_opening_the_tap_goes_live_when_the_writer_dies_at_birth.
  Line-neutral.
